% Versioned rules: a claim is judged by the LCD version in effect on its date
% of service. The CGM criteria of L33822 changed on 18 July 2021 and on 16
% April 2023; the refill contact window of every DME MAC LCD on 1 January
% 2024 (dmepos.le). The earlier versions are read from the revision history
% the Medicare Coverage Database export keeps (sources/history/), which
% quotes the wording each revision removed.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base glucose versions includes these resources:
    glucose_monitors.

the knowledge base glucose versions includes:

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query refills is:
    the refill requirements are met for which claim.

% Bea takes one insulin administration a day and is trained on her CGM. Her
% CGM claim of 1 March 2023 falls under the criteria of July 2021 (three or
% more administrations or a pump): not covered. The same device on 1 June
% 2023 falls under the criteria of April 2023 (insulin-treated): covered.
scenario cgm_one_daily_administration is:
    claim 1 is for the March CGM.
    the HCPCS code of the March CGM is "E2103".
    the March CGM is furnished to Bea.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2023-03-01.
    the order for the March CGM is dated 2023-02-20.
    the March CGM is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    claim 2 is for the June CGM.
    the HCPCS code of the June CGM is "E2103".
    the June CGM is furnished to Bea.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2023-06-01.
    the order for the June CGM is dated 2023-05-20.
    the June CGM is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    the diagnosis code of Bea is "E11.9".
    Bea is currently being treated with insulin.
    Bea is treated with 1 daily administrations of insulin.
    the finding trained on continuous glucose monitor about Bea is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Bea to evaluate diabetes control on 2023-02-10.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Bea to evaluate diabetes control on 2023-05-10.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Cal takes four administrations a day and adjusts his doses on his readings.
% In 2022 that suffices; before 18 July 2021 he also had to test four times a
% day, and the record says three.
scenario cgm_testing_frequency_before_2021 is:
    claim 1 is for the 2021 CGM.
    the HCPCS code of the 2021 CGM is "K0554".
    the 2021 CGM is furnished to Cal.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2021-03-01.
    the order for the 2021 CGM is dated 2021-02-20.
    the 2021 CGM is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    claim 2 is for the 2022 CGM.
    the HCPCS code of the 2022 CGM is "K0554".
    the 2022 CGM is furnished to Cal.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2022-03-01.
    the order for the 2022 CGM is dated 2022-02-20.
    the 2022 CGM is prescribed in accordance with its FDA indications for use.
    the diagnosis code of Cal is "E10.9".
    Cal is currently being treated with insulin.
    Cal is treated with 4 daily administrations of insulin.
    Cal tests blood glucose 3 times per day.
    the finding insulin regimen requires frequent self adjustment about Cal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Cal to evaluate diabetes control on 2021-02-10.
    the treating practitioner had an in-person or telehealth visit with Cal to evaluate diabetes control on 2022-02-10.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Refills: the beneficiary confirmed 20 days before the shipping date, the
% supply ending 5 days after it. Under the rule before 1 January 2024 (no
% sooner than 14 days before shipping) the December 2023 refill fails; under
% the current rule (within 30 days of the expected end) the February 2024
% one passes.
scenario refill_window_change is:
    claim 1 is for the December strips.
    the HCPCS code of the December strips is "A4253".
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2023-12-20.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the December strips on 2023-11-30.
    the current supply of the December strips is expected to end on 2023-12-25.
    claim 2 is for the February strips.
    the HCPCS code of the February strips is "A4253".
    claim 2 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2024-02-20.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the February strips on 2024-01-31.
    the current supply of the February strips is expected to end on 2024-02-25.
    refills expects answers ["the refill requirements are met for claim 2"].
